hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20969","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: An elder sat to us in the place of Ayyub, and he heard the people narrating, so he said: My master narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: What is his name. He said: Qurrah ibn Damos al-Numayri. He said: I came to Madinah and went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with people around him, and I kept wanting to approach him but could not, so I called to him: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for the Numayri boy. He said: May Allah forgive you. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent al-Dahhak ibn Qays as a collector, and when he returned he returned with full-grown camels. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did you go to Hilal ibn Amir and Numayr ibn Amir and Amir ibn Rabiah and take the best of their wealth. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard you mention raiding, so I wanted to bring you camels to ride and carry upon. He said: By Allah, what you left is dearer to me than what you took. Return them and take from the edges of their wealth their charities. He said: I heard the Muslims calling those camels the aged strivers."
